en and the  red  graphs there but the high chip  data contains long-range interaction  information  that is shown by the arcs below the  green line  the green graph and each of those arcs  represent  an interaction in three-dimensional  space between  different ctsc ctcf molecules  not only that we can zoom in to a  specific ctcf  binding site and what you can see is  that compared to the chipseek data  the positioning of the nucleosomes  within that data set  is extremely clear as depicted by  the the peaks and valleys as i shared  with in that previous slide  now this assay is very easy to get up  and  running in the lab we have a panel of  pre-validated antibodies that are  available for it  to get you going before i finish out i  just wanted to share  one perspective in terms of how one  might start  using these different products in trying  to understand various aspects of  gene expression here we're looking at an  omni-c data set where we've  mapped the different a and b  compartments as shown by  the orange and the red tracks there  labeled pc1  where they are positive above the line  is an a compartment where they're below  the line is a b  compartment what you can see comparing  brain to liver is  there are differences between the two  and those  map to specific changes in  methylation of the histones as well as  gene expression changes  so just to finish up here hopefully what  i've convinced you of  is there's a variety of different  dovetail kits  that are available all of which use  sequence independent  nuclear endonucleases to help  maximize the data that one is getting  from your studies to address  a variety of different applications  including structural variant detection  and intel genotyping genome assembly  apple type phasing  and genome conformation with that i'm  going to stop here thank you for your  attention  and would be very happy to address any  questions you might have
 

